# 🛰 Request Logger Middleware

A fullstack project that implements custom HTTP request logging middleware using **Express.js** and a **React** frontend to trigger and visualize requests in real time.

---

## 📋 Table of Contents

- [Overview](#overview)
- [Project Structure](#project-structure)
- [Tech Stack](#tech-stack)
- [Getting Started](#getting-started)
- [How the Middleware Works](#how-the-middleware-works)
- [API Endpoints](#api-endpoints)
- [Example Output](#example-output)

---

## Overview

This project demonstrates how middleware works in Express.js. Every incoming HTTP request is intercepted and logged with:

- **Timestamp** — `HH:MM:SS` format
- **HTTP Method** — `GET`, `POST`, `DELETE`, etc.
- **Request URL** — `/user`, `/products`, etc.

**Example log output:**
```
10:30:22 GET /user
10:31:05 POST /orders
10:31:47 DELETE /user/42
```

---

## Project Structure

```
project/
├── server/
│   ├── index.js                  # Express server entry point
│   └── middleware/
│       └── logger.js             # Custom logging middleware
└── client/
    └── src/
        └── App.jsx               # React frontend
```

